#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:53
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Computer users have a very large amount of data to manage, some of which is "
"sensitive. In particular, you will typically have many passwords to manage. "
"Remembering them is difficult, writing them down on paper or in a text file "
"is insecure, and using tools such at PGP is tedious and inconvenient."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kwallet; saves this sensitive data for you in a strongly encrypted "
"<footnote><para> The data is encrypted with the <ulink url=\"http://www."
"schneier.com/blowfish.html\">Blowfish symmetric block cipher algorithm</"
"ulink>, the algorithm key is derived from the <ulink url=\"http://www.ietf."
"org/rfc/rfc3174.txt\">SHA-1 hash</ulink> of the password, with a key length "
"of 156 bits (20 bytes). The data into the wallet file is also hashed with "
"SHA-1 and checked before the data is deciphered and accessible by the "
"applications. </para></footnote> file, accessible by all applications, and "
"protected with a master password that you define."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kwallet; supports multiple wallets, so for the most secure operation, you "
"should use one wallet for local passwords, and another for network passwords "
"and form data. You can configure this behavior in the &kwallet; "
"&systemsettings; module, however the default setting is to store everything "
"in one wallet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A wallet is by default closed, which means that you must supply a password "
"to open it. Once the wallet is opened, the contents can be accessed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &kwallet;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you visit &eg; the &kde; bugtracker and enter the login data for the "
"first time, a dialog pops up offering to store the password in an encrypted "
"wallet:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Request to save login information</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Request to save login information</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to store this information, select <guibutton>Store</guibutton> "
"to proceed. In case you did not create a wallet so far, the next dialog asks "
"for the wallet password and creates a wallet named kdewallet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Create a wallet</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Create a wallet</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Next time you visit the same website again, the application requests to open "
"the wallet. Enter the wallet password and click the <guibutton>Open</"
"guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Request to open a wallet</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Request to open a wallet</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This connects the application to the wallet, enables it to read the login "
"data from the wallet and to restore the login information for this website. "
"Once an application is connected to the wallet, it can automatically restore "
"any login information stored in the wallet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kwalletmanager;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kwalletmanager; serves a number of functions. Firstly it allows you to see "
"if any wallets are open, which wallets those are, and which applications are "
"using each wallet. You can disconnect an application's access to a wallet "
"from within the &kwalletmanager;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may also manage the wallets installed on the system, creating and "
"deleting wallets and manipulating their contents (changing keys, ...)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kwalletmanager; application is launched with <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Applications</guimenu><guisubmenu>System</guisubmenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Wallet Management Tool</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the "
"application launcher. Alternatively start &krunner; with shortcut <keycombo "
"action=\"simul\">&Alt;<keycap>F2</keycap></keycombo> and enter "
"<command>kwalletmanager</command>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A system tray icon indicates that a wallet is open: <mediaobject> "
"<imageobject> <imagedata fileref=\"oxygen48-status-wallet-open.png\"/> </"
"imageobject> </mediaobject> When all wallets are closed, the icon will "
"reflect this by showing a closed wallet:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:170
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click once on the system tray wallet icon to display the &kwalletmanager; "
"window showing all available wallets as icons which reflect their current "
"status, either open or closed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kwalletmanager; Context Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<mousebutton>Right</mousebutton> clicking on a wallet in the "
"&kwalletmanager; window offers the following functions:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid "New Wallet..."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Create a new wallet. A dialog box will ask you for the name of the new "
"wallet that you want to create."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycap>Return</keycap></shortcut> <guisubmenu>Open...</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Open the wallet. Opening the wallet causes the contents of the wallet to be "
"displayed in a new window where you can add, delete, or modify the contents "
"of the wallet. You may also double click the wallet icon to cause it to "
"open. If the wallet is not already open, you will be requested to enter the "
"password. See below for details of using the wallet window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:213
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Change Password"
msgid "Change Password..."
msgstr "Modificar lo mot de pas"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid "Change the master password for the wallet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guisubmenu
#: index.docbook:220
#, no-c-format
msgid "Disconnect"
msgstr "Desconnectar"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Disconnect an application from the wallet. Currently connected applications "
"will appear in a submenu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>W</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenuitem>Close</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "Force the wallet to be closed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:233
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycap>Del</keycap></shortcut><guimenuitem>Delete</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:235
#, no-c-format
msgid "Delete the wallet"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Wallet Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:244
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Double clicking on a wallet in the &kwalletmanager; window will open a new "
"window displaying that wallet's contents. A wallet may contain any number of "
"folders, which allow storing of password information. By default a wallet "
"will contain folders named Form Data and Passwords."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid "The window has three sections:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:260
#, no-c-format
msgid "A search line to filter the items of the current wallet"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:262
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The tree view of the folders contained in the wallet. Click the <guiicon>&gt;"
"</guiicon> / <guiicon>v</guiicon> symbols to expand or collapse the tree "
"view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:265
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The contents of the selected folder entry at the right side. By default the "
"password and value are hidden. To display and edit them enable "
"<guilabel>Show values</guilabel> or click the <guilabel>Show Contents</"
"guilabel> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:271
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Folders may be added, deleted or renamed via the context menu, and selecting "
"a folder will update the folder entry list and the summary display. "
"Selecting a folder entry will update the entry contents pane, and allow you "
"to edit that entry."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:283
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Entries may also be created or deleted via the context menu for the folder "
"contents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:286
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All folders and entries may be dragged and dropped into other wallets or "
"folders respectively. This allows a user to easily package up a new wallet "
"for transfer to another environment. For instance, a new wallet could be "
"created and copied onto a removable flash memory device. Important passwords "
"could be transferred there, so you have them available in other locations."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:294
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adding Entries Manually"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:295
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Open the context menu with the &RMB; click on <guilabel>Maps</guilabel> or "
"<guilabel>Passwords</guilabel> in the <guilabel>Folder</guilabel> tree view. "
"Select <guimenuitem>New</guimenuitem> and choose a name for the new entry."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:298
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the folder contents pane select <guilabel>New Entry</guilabel> from the "
"context menu. For passwords click the <guilabel>Show Contents</guilabel> "
"button, enter the new password. For Maps you have to add a <guilabel>Key</"
"guilabel> and a <guilabel>Value</guilabel>. Click the <guilabel>Save</"
"guilabel> button to store the new entries in the encrypted wallet file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:312
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring &kwallet;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:315
#, no-c-format
msgid "Wallet Preferences"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kwallet; contains a small configuration panel with several options that "
"allow you to tune &kwallet; to your personal preferences. The default "
"settings for &kwallet; are sufficient for most users."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:321
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Check the box to enable or disable the &kde; wallet subsystem entirely. If "
"this box is unchecked, then &kwallet; is entirely disabled and none of the "
"other options here have any effect, nor will &kwallet; record any "
"information, or offer to fill in forms for you."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid "Close Wallet"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:329
#, no-c-format
msgid "Close when unused for:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:331
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Close the current wallet after a period of inactivity. If you check this "
"option, set the period in the box, default is 10 minutes. When a wallet is "
"closed, the password is needed to access it again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:338
#, no-c-format
msgid "Close when screensaver starts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:340
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Close the wallet as soon as the screen saver starts. When a wallet is "
"closed, the password is needed to access it again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid "Close when last application stops using it"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:348
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Close the wallet as soon as applications that use it have stopped. Note that "
"your wallets will only be closed when all the applications that use it have "
"stopped. When a wallet is closed, the password is needed to access it again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:357
#, no-c-format
msgid "Automatic Wallet Selection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:359
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select wallet to use as default:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:361
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select which wallet you want to use as default wallet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:366
#, no-c-format
msgid "Different wallet for local passwords:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:368
#, no-c-format
msgid "If checked, choose a different wallet for local passwords."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:374
#, no-c-format
msgid "Wallet Manager"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:376
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show manager in system tray"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:378
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enable the wallet manager to have its icon in the system tray."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid "Hide System tray icon when last wallet closes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:386
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When there is no wallet in use anymore, remove the wallet icon from the "
"system tray."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:392
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Finally, there is a button labeled <guibutton>Launch Wallet Manager</"
"guibutton>, which does precisely that."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid "This button is only visible if &kwalletmanager; is not running"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:398
#, no-c-format
msgid "Access Control"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:400
#, no-c-format
msgid "There is only one option on this page:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:404
#, no-c-format
msgid "Prompt when an application accesses a wallet"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:406
#, no-c-format
msgid "Signal you when an application gains access to a wallet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:411
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Next there is a tree style view of the access controls for your wallets."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:413
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click with the &LMB; on the <guiicon>&gt;</guiicon> symbol beside a wallet "
"name to expand the tree. You will see the name of each application that has "
"asked for access to the wallet, and the policy you set for it. You cannot "
"edit policies here, or add them, but it is possible to delete an entry by "
"&RMB; clicking on it and choosing <guimenuitem>Delete</guimenuitem> from the "
"context menu that appears, or by simply selecting it and pressing the "
"<keysym>Del</keysym> key."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:421
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"An application that has been allowed access to a wallet is granted access to "
"all passwords stored inside."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:492
#, no-c-format
msgid "Advanced Features"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:494
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Wallets can be dragged from the &kwalletmanager; window. This allows you to "
"drag the wallet to a file browser window, where you can choose to copy, "
"move, or link the wallet, as desired."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:498
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You might use this to save a wallet to portable media, such as a USB "
"keychain, so that you can take your passwords with you to work or on a "
"vacation, and still have easy access to important sites."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:502
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Future versions will have built-in functions for easy export or copying of "
"data to portable devices."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:506
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Information on the internal structure of &kwallet; and some useful links to "
"the code where you can find the answers on questions about the structure of "
"the passwords records and the ciphers applied to keep passwords confident "
"can be found on <ulink url=\"http://techbase.kde.org/Projects/Utils/kwallet"
"\">&kwallet; TechBase page</ulink>."
msgstr ""

